-- title:
--   Finiteness and separability of the modular function field over K(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $N \ge 1$ an integer. Write $j =$ `jqModC K` for the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\,\eta^{-\mathrm{unit}})$ over $K$, i.e. the image in $K(\!(q)\!)$ of the integral $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and $j_N =$ `jqNModC K N` for its image under the ring homomorphism `qExpand K N` that multiplies all exponents by $N$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^N$). Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N` be the intermediate field $K(j, j_N)$ of $K(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $K$ by these two series. Given a packet `data : ModularPolynomialData N`, consisting of a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$ in $Y$ with $\Phi(j, j_N) = 0$, and assuming that $j_N$ is separable over the subfield $K(j)$ of $K(\!(q)\!)$ (its minimal polynomial there is separable), the conclusion is: the element $j$, viewed inside $F$, generates a subfield $K\langle j\rangle \subseteq F$ over which $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable as an algebra.
--
--   This is the statement that the level-$N$ modular function field in characteristic-free form is a finite separable extension of the rational subfield generated by $j$, so that $j$ is a separating transcendence element for it. It serves as the input for treating $F$ as the function field of a curve over $K$ with $j$ as coordinate, and is used downstream in the construction of models and places of the modular curve and in the theory of mod $p$ forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finiteDimensional_and_isSeparable_adjoin_jGeomGen_of_isSeparable_jqNModC.lean

